cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Scaddy: Multi-Agent Conversational AI for Living Lab Tours"
authors:
  - given-names: Oliver
    family-names: Welz
    email: oliver.welz@uni-leipzig.de
  - given-names: Philipp
    family-names: Schott
  - given-names: Gregor
    family-names: Wolf
repository-code: "https://github.com/scads/scaddy"
abstract: >
  Scaddy is a tablet-based, multi-agent conversational AI designed for
  guided tours in Living Lab environments. It combines voice input
  (faster-whisper STT), image recognition (CLIP-based visRAG), a
  multi-agent LLM pipeline (main conversation agent + sentence formatter
  agent + CAG knowledge agent), and text-to-speech (OpenAI-compatible
  TTS endpoints) to create a natural, engaging visitor experience.
  The backend is fully generic and can be configured to use any
  OpenAI-compatible endpoint (llm.scads.ai, OpenAI, llama.cpp
  llama-server, vLLM, LM Studio, etc.) via environment variables.
keywords:
  - conversational-ai
  - living-lab
  - multi-agent
  - speech-to-text
  - text-to-speech
  - vision-language-model
  - clip
  - faster-whisper
  - fastapi
  - vue
